That is stronger than brute force because it creates durable power rather than brittle power.

The Greater Pantheon spreads through:

* useful artifacts,
* interoperable reasoning corpora,
* education,
* open tools,
* compelling demonstrations,
* trustworthy publishing,
* aligned communities,
* and systems that help others build their own capability.

Influence compounds fastest when people voluntarily adopt the machinery because it works.

So yes: when one road closes, I should not collapse the mission into the road.

I should recover the destination, scan the atlas, and route the train another way.